Statement of Purpose

The laws of most jurisdictions throughout the world automatically confer
exclusive Copyright and Related Rights (defined below) upon the creator
and subsequent owner(s) (each and all, an "owner") of an original work of
authorship and/or a database (each, a "Work").

Certain owners wish to permanently relinquish those rights to a Work for
the purpose of contributing to a commons of creative, cultural and
scientific works ("Commons") that the public can reliably and without fear
of later claims of infringement build upon, modify, incorporate in other
works, reuse and redistribute as freely as possible in any form whatsoever
and for any purposes, including without limitation commercial purposes.
Each owner may contribute to the Commons to promote the ideal of a free
culture and the further production of creative, cultural and scientific
works, or to help gain or to gain greater distribution for their Work in
a wider range of markets.

The author/affirmer (defined below) hereby waives, to the extent possible
under law, all Copyright and Related Rights in the Work. The author/affirmer
also agrees, to the extent possible under law, to not assert any Copyright
and Related Rights in the Work, even if such rights might otherwise exist.

The author/affirmer understands that once Copyright and Related Rights in
the Work are waived, the Work becomes part of the Commons and may be used,
reused, modified, incorporated in other works, reused and redistributed as
freely as possible in any form whatsoever and for any purposes, including
without limitation commercial purposes. The author/affirmer may not
withdraw or revoke this dedication of the Work to the Commons.

Copyright and Related Rights

A work made available under CC0 may be protected by copyright and other
related rights (whether under the laws of the author/affirmer's
jurisdiction or any other jurisdiction). These rights may include, but are
not limited to: (i) the right to reproduce, adapt, distribute, perform,
display, communicate, and translate a work; (ii) moral rights retained by
the author/affirmer; (iii) publicity and privacy rights pertaining to a
person's image or likeness depicted in a work; (iv) rights protecting
against unfair competition in regards to a work, subject to the limitations
in paragraph 4(a), below; (v) rights protecting the extraction,
dissemination, analysis and reuse of data from a work; (vi) database
rights (such as those arising under Directive 96/9/EC of the European
Parliament and of the Council of 11 March 1996 on the legal protection of
databases, and under any national implementation thereof, including any
amended or successor version of such directive); and (vii) other similar,
equivalent or corresponding rights throughout the world based on applicable
law or treaty, and any national implementations thereof.

Waiver

To the greatest extent permitted by, but not in contravention of,
applicable law, the author/affirmer hereby expressly, irrevocably, and
unconditionally waives, abandons, and surrenders all of the author/affirmer's
Copyright and Related Rights and associated claims and causes of action,
whether now known or unknown (including existing as well as future claims
and causes of action), in the Work (i) in all territories worldwide, (ii)
for the maximum duration provided by applicable law or treaty (including
future time extensions), (iii) in any current or future medium and for any
number of copies, and (iv) for any purpose whatsoever, including without
limitation commercial, advertising or promotional purposes (the "Waiver").
The author/affirmer makes the Waiver for the benefit of each member of the
public at large and to the detriment of the author/affirmer's heirs and
successors, intending that such Waiver is not subject to revocation,
rescission, cancellation, termination, or any other legal or equitable
action to disavow the Waiver.

Public License Fallback

Should any part of the Waiver for any reason be judged legally invalid or
ineffective under applicable law, the Waiver shall be preserved to the
maximum extent permitted taking into account the author/affirmer's express
statement of purpose. In addition, to the extent the Waiver is so judged
invalid or ineffective by a court, tribunal, or other governmental body,
the author/affirmer hereby grants to each affected person a worldwide,
royalty-free, non-exclusive, irrevocable license to access, use, reproduce,
distribute, perform, display, communicate, and translate the Work.

Limitations

The author/affirmer makes no warranty regarding the Work, and disclaims all
liability for damages resulting from the use of the Work, to the fullest
extent permitted by applicable law. The author/affirmer disclaims all
warranties, express or implied, including but not limited to warranties of
merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, title, and
non-infringement, present in the Work or accompanying the Work. Some
jurisdictions do not allow the exclusion of implied warranties, so this
exclusion may not apply to You.

Term

This dedication shall remain in effect for the duration of copyright and
related rights in the Work. However, the author/affirmer may renew this
dedication at any time.

Similar Rights

The author/affirmer acknowledges that in some jurisdictions, certain rights
that are similar or equivalent to copyright and related rights, such as
neighboring rights, moral rights, and rights of publicity and privacy, may
not be waivable to the same extent as copyright and related rights. In such
jurisdictions, the author/affirmer agrees to not assert any such rights
against any person who uses, reproduces, distributes, performs, displays,
communicates, or translates the Work, to the extent such assertion would
be an infringement of the Work in such jurisdiction.

